  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> characteristics of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction diode in forward bias is shown in the figure. The ratio of dynamic resistance, corresponding to forward bias voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respective is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0088_8b6f17c04ae3.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 166px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>40</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Dynamic resistance of a diode is defined as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0088_8b6f17c04ae3.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 159px;\" /></p><p>At forward bias voltage of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>At forward bias voltage of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>250</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}